CodeSystem: AHIPDemoDisabilityCodes
Id: ahip-demo-disability-codes
Title: "AHIP Demo Disability Codes"
Description: "AHIP-specific codes identifying functional difficulty categories used to determine disability status across activities of daily living."
* insert DEMoStandardMetadata
* ^language = #en
* ^version = "0.0.1"
* ^status = #active
* ^date = "2025-03-25T00:00:00-04:00"
* ^content = #complete
* ^caseSensitive = true
* ^experimental = false

* #HEAR "Hearing" "Deafness or serious difficulty hearing because of a physical or mental health condition."
* #SEEI "Seeing (even when wearing glasses)" "Blindness or serious difficulty seeing, even when wearing glasses, because of a physical or mental health condition."
* #WALK "Walking or climbing stairs" "Serious difficulty walking or climbing stairs because of a physical or mental health condition."
* #CONC "Concentrating, remembering, or making decisions" "Serious difficulty concentrating, remembering, or making decisions because of a physical or mental health condition."
* #DRES "Dressing or bathing" "Difficulty dressing or bathing because of a physical or mental health condition."
* #COOK "Cooking for oneself" "Difficulty cooking for oneself because of a physical or mental health condition."
* #FEED "Feeding oneself" "Difficulty feeding oneself because of a physical or mental health condition."
* #TOIL "Using the toilet" "Difficulty using the toilet because of a physical or mental health condition."
* #ERRA "Doing errands alone, such as shopping or visiting a doctor’s office" "Difficulty doing errands alone, such as shopping or visiting a doctor's office, because of a physical or mental health condition."
* #COMM "Communicating or being understood using your usual language" "Difficulty communicating or being understood using one's usual language because of a physical or mental health condition."
* #UNDE "Understanding when someone speaks in your usual language" "Difficulty understanding when someone speaks in one's usual language because of a physical or mental health condition."
